      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The study of two novel drugs for management of both painful and silent myocardial ischemia isosorbide-5-mononitrate (IS-5-MN), efox, and its long-acting variant efox-long demonstrated that both drugs exerted noticeable antianginal effect at maximal concentration in blood. This was achieved by a single dose and course administration. The differences in the effects of the two dosage forms of IS-5-MN on painless ischemia may be explained by limited coronary reserves of anginal patients."},
